{"entry":{"active":true,"body":"Azhdarcho\nAzhdarcho /ɑːʒˈdɑrxoʊ/ is a genus of pterodactyloid pterosaur from the late Cretaceous Period of the Bissekty Formation (middle Turonian stage, about 92 million years ago) of Uzbekistan. It is known from fragmentary remains including the distinctive, elongated neck vertebrae that characterizes members of the family Azhdarchidae, which also includes such giant pterosaurs as Quetzalcoatlus.","memory":1000002,"scope":2,"seq":0},"permission_revision":1,"read_seq":0,"retrieval_mode":"historical_state","validated_at_seq":1}
